[Music]  the newest version of the Grinch is  cleaning up at the box office it raked  in 66 million dollars its first weekend  that makes it the biggest opening for  any Christmas movie ever breaking the  record set by the live-action version of  the story 18 years ago starring Jim  Carrey and that film was of course a  remake of the 1966 TV special How the  Grinch Stole Christmas so at this point  you're probably wondering did we really  need another Grinch movie we're here to  break down all the biggest differences  between the three versions and tell you  which one is the best let's start with  what we can see the character design of  the newest Grinch is pretty novel even  besides the fact that he's 3d animated  take a look at the original Grinch the  one practically ripped from the pages of  the dr. Seuss book he had a sinister  look to him with a wrinkly Cheshire Cat  like sneer Jim Carrey's Grinch was even  creepier as heavy makeup and prosthetics  gave him a snout nose in an overall  wolfish look in contrasts our new Grinch  is almost cute you can see each  individual animated hair on his body  giving him a furry looking texture that  fuzziness combined with his full round  cheeks and pear-shaped body turn this  Grinch into a surprisingly cuddly  creature looking at them next to each  other you can really see how  illumination the animation studio behind  this newest version gave Grinch a look  that's in line with some of their other  projects like the Lorax and Despicable  Me next let's take a look at the man  himself his inner workings and  motivations in the original picture book  an animated film  Zeus didn't give any reason for grinches  hatred of the holidays beyond the fact  that his heart was two sizes too small  that's not a ton of character  development the live-action movie did  provide a window into the past showing a  young Grinch being bullied by his  classmates but in that version he also  exhibited heartless tendencies from the  start even when he was just a baby  this year's origin story makes it clear  that the Grinch started out wide-eyed  and hopeful like any other kid  but growing up in an orphanage where he  spent the holidays alone year after year  slowly eroded his confidence and  compassion feeling alienated from the  cheery whois of Whoville he became a  recluse who just wants to hang out with  his dog and avoid the holidays  altogether and you really can't blame  him  the Grinch's pass is taken far more  seriously here than in the Jim Carrey  film and we can easily see why he's so  embittered now let's look at some other  characters Cindy Lou who gets some added  depth in the newest remake in both the  previous films Cindy Lou comes from a  two-parent home in the live-action  version her parents get caught up in the  materialism of the holiday season which  bothers her in this version Cindy Lou  isn't motivated by materialism but by  concern for her overworked single mom  Donna who's voiced by rashida Jones  co-director Y ro Cheney told Insider  about the decision to make Donna a  single parent saying we didn't want that  place and needs people to see him just  saccharine a postcard version of a happy  Christmas town we wanted it to feel like  a real place with real people with real  problems ok time to talk about the music  it's something that you may not  automatically think about but that  played a big role in all three movies  the soundtrack to the new film spans  several genres futuring songs by the  Jackson 5 Run DMC and the hip hop  boyband Brock Hampton meanwhile rapper  Tyler the Creator put his own catchy  take on the original theme song  [Music]  Tyler also released a boisterous EP of  holiday music for the Grinch which  perfectly complements the mischievous  humor and Bray animation of the film the  live-action version had its own hit song  where are you Christmas an original  track that was co-written by Mariah  Carey little Taylor Momsen sings a sweet  rendition of the song as Cindy Lou Who  well country superstar Faith Hill  released an official recording and music  video it peaked at number 26 on the US  Billboard country charts  and has no doubt been belted in showers  for years after the movie's release the  first film though offered a truly iconic  and unique addition to holiday music  with the original version of you're a  mean one mr. Grinch mr. Grinch it was  sung by booming bass vocalists Thurl  Ravenscroft and has since been covered  by tons of folks including Jim Carrey as  the Grinch and even the cast of Glee  finally let's look at what audience and  critics have to say there's no  Metacritic score for the original  because it was released so long ago  audiences though gave it an 8 point 4  out of 10 but let's take that with the  grain of salt  these reviews poured in way after the  release so surely a bit of nostalgia is  at play here the 2000 jump carry version  has a 6 point 1 out of 10 from audiences  and only a 45% on Metacritic ouch this  year's version only fared slightly  better with a 6 point 3 audience score  out of 10 and a 53% critics score so  which one is the best I'd say this  year's version because it feels like a  fully modern update on the Yuletide  classic the newest take on the film  feels truly different and not just  because it's the first 3d animated  Grinch movie we get a new perspective on  everyone's favorite green Grouch as  illumination gives him a charming new  look and a deeper origin story at the  end even with all its departures from  earlier versions of the Grinch the movie  stays rooted and Seuss's basic message  about empathy and redemption through  community  [Music]

